// Hive-partition cases that also filter on a PAYLOAD column, not just the path-derived partition
// column. Kept apart from external-hive-partitioned.csv-spec because this shape once failed inside the
// reader with "output schema size [1] does not match mapping width" -- elastic/esql-planning#1769.
//
// That defect is FIXED (elastic/elasticsearch#157982), and NDJSON now returns the right count here. The
// file stays separate for a different reason: NDJSON also emits a warning no other format does, because
// it omits absent keys entirely, so `languages` is genuinely missing from some files. A shared spec
// declares one warning set for every format that runs it, so NDJSON cannot join this one. Its copy of
// the case, with the warning declared, lives in ndjson-sparse-columns.csv-spec.
//
// Routing: ORC, Parquet and parquet-rs glob external-*.csv-spec and pick this up; TSV names it
// explicitly. NDJSON's absence is declared in fixture-matrix.properties rather than left implicit.

hivePartitionConsistentWithPayload
required_capability: dataset_in_from_command
dataset: employees_hive: "{{employees_hive}}"

FROM employees_hive
| WHERE lang IS NULL AND languages IS NULL
| STATS count = COUNT(*);

count:long
10
;
